<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Probability of an event from a bag of bottle tops</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>A bag holds \({@r@}\) red, \({@g@}\) green, \({@w@}\) white and \({@y@}\) yellow bottle tops. {@nm@} takes one bottle top at random.</p><p>Give each probability exactly, as a fraction or an exact decimal.</p><p>(a) Find \(P(\text{red})\).</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find \(P(\text{not green})\).</p><div>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Find \(P(\text{red or white})\).</p><div>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>There are \({@r@} + {@g@} + {@w@} + {@y@} = {@N@}\) bottle tops, and each is equally likely to be taken. Count the bottle tops that make the event happen and divide by \({@N@}\).</p><p>(a) \(P(\text{red}) = \dfrac{{@r@}}{{@N@}} = {@ta1@}\).</p><p>(b) An event either happens or it does not, so the two probabilities add to 1. \(P(\text{not green}) = 1 - \dfrac{{@g@}}{{@N@}} = \dfrac{{@N-g@}}{{@N@}} = {@ta2@}\).</p><p>(c) One bottle top cannot be both red and white, so count both colours together: \(P(\text{red or white}) = \dfrac{{@r@} + {@w@}}{{@N@}} = \dfrac{{@r+w@}}{{@N@}} = {@ta3@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* pdec: exact decimal display of a value with at most 4 decimal places */
pdec(v) := if integerp(v) then v elseif integerp(10*v) then dispdp(float(v),1) elseif integerp(100*v) then dispdp(float(v),2) elseif integerp(1000*v) then dispdp(float(v),3) else dispdp(float(v),4);
/* Design: probability of each colour and "not", with four colours and an "or" part. Curated lists. Source: adapted from SMP GCSE Foundation book 1, chapter 19, section A, A5. */
L: [[8,4,3,7],[7,4,9,5],[4,2,7,9],[4,7,8,2],[6,3,8,4],[3,2,9,6],[3,7,4,5],[5,8,6,2],[4,6,3,5],[7,8,3,4]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
nm: rand(["Akoth","Kiprotich","Zawadi"]);
r: L[ix][1]; g: L[ix][2]; w: L[ix][3]; y: L[ix][4];
N: r+g+w+y;
ta1: r/N; ta2: (N-g)/N; ta3: (r+w)/N;
tl1: min(1/200,ta1/20); tl2: min(1/200,ta2/20); tl3: min(1/200,ta3/20);
/* diagnostics */
odds1: r/(N-r);
dg2: g/N;
half3: (r+w)/(2*N);
prod3: r*w/N^2;]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
