  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Probability III: probability of an event by counting</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Essential 3.2: Find probabilities of single events, a complement and an 'or' event for one draw from a bag, by counting equally likely outcomes.</p><p id="edition">Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 19, Section A, question A5 of Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP GCSE Mathematics: Foundation 1 for AQA, Edexcel and OCR two-tier GCSE mathematics, Cambridge University Press, 2006: four colours, a complement part and an 'or' part, randomised, with a new Kenyan context and new numbers.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
